      "text": "To find the value of \\((1+r)(1+s)(1+t)\\) where \\(r, s, t\\) are the roots of the polynomial \\(x^3 - 20x^2 + 18x - 7 = 0\\), we can use Vieta's formulas. Vieta's formulas relate the coefficients of the polynomial to sums and products of its roots.\n\nFor the polynomial \\(x^3 - 20x^2 + 18x - 7 = 0\\), Vieta's formulas tell us:\n\\[\nr + s + t = 20,\n\\]\n\\[\nrs + rt + st = 18,\n\\]\n\\[\nrst = 7.\n\\]\n\nWe need to find the value of \\((1+r)(1+s)(1+t)\\). First, expand the expression \\((1+r)(1+s)(1+t)\\):\n\\[\n(1+r)(1+s)(1+t) = 1 + r + s + t + rs + rt + st + rt + rs + st + rst.\n\\]\nThis simplifies to:\n\\[\n1 + r + s + t + 3(rs + rt + st) + rst.\n\\]\nSubstitute the values from Vieta's formulas into the expression:\n\\[\n1 + 20 + 3(18) + 7.\n\\]\nCalculate the terms:\n\\[\n1 + 20 + 54 + 7 = 82.\n\\]\nTherefore, the value of \\((1+r)(1+s)(1+t)\\) is \\(\\boxed{82}\\).",
