      "text": "To find the value of \\((1+r)(1+s)(1+t)\\) where \\(r, s, t\\) are the roots of the polynomial \\(x^3 - 20x^2 + 18x - 7 = 0\\), we can use the relationships between the roots and coefficients of the polynomial.\n\nFirst, recall Vieta's formulas for the roots of the polynomial \\(x^3 + ax^2 + bx + c = 0\\). For the polynomial \\(x^3 - 20x^2 + 18x - 7 = 0\\), we have:\n- The sum of the roots \\(r + s + t = 20\\),\n- The sum of the product of the roots taken two at a time \\(rs + rt + st = 18\\),\n- The product of the roots \\(rst = 7\\).\n\nWe need to find the value of \\((1+r)(1+s)(1+t)\\). Expanding this product, we get:\n\\[\n(1+r)(1+s)(1+t) = 1 + r + s + t + rs + rt + st + rt + st + rst.\n\\]\nSubstituting the values from Vieta's formulas, we have:\n\\[\n(1+r)(1+s)(1+t) = 1 + (r+s+t) + (rs+rt+st) + rst.\n\\]\nWe know from Vieta's formulas that \\(r + s + t = 20\\), \\(rs + rt + st = 18\\), and \\(rst = 7\\). Substituting these values in, we get:\n\\[\n(1+r)(1+s)(1+t) = 1 + 20 + 18 + 7 = 46.\n\\]\nTherefore, the value of \\((1+r)(1+s)(1+t)\\) is \\(\\boxed{46}\\).",
