      "text": "To solve for \\((1+r)(1+s)(1+t)\\), we can use the properties of the roots of the polynomial equation. Given that \\(r\\), \\(s\\), and \\(t\\) are the roots of the polynomial equation \\(x^3 - 20x^2 + 18x - 7 = 0\\), we can use Vieta's formulas, which relate the coefficients of the polynomial to sums and products of its roots. According to Vieta's formulas, for a cubic polynomial \\(x^3 + ax^2 + bx + c = 0\\), the sum of the roots \\(r + s + t\\) is equal to \\(-a\\), the sum of the product of the roots taken two at a time \\(rs + rt + st\\) is equal to \\(b\\), and the product of the roots \\(rst\\) is equal to \\(-c\\). For the polynomial \\(x^3 - 20x^2 + 18x - 7 = 0\\), we have:\n\\[ r + s + t = 20, \\]\n\\[ rs + rt + st = 18, \\]\n\\[ rst = 7. \\]\n\nWe need to find the value of \\((1+r)(1+s)(1+t)\\). Expanding the expression, we get:\n\\[ (1+r)(1+s)(1+t) = 1 + r + s + t + rs + rt + st + rst. \\]\nSubstituting the values from Vieta's formulas, we have:\n\\[ (1+r)(1+s)(1+t) = 1 + 20 + 18 + 7 = 46. \\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\((1+r)(1+s)(1+t)\\) is \\(\\boxed{46}\\).",
